tools.description:
Compute a saved project locally with the same CPU Worker as the browser. Writes the full analysis to outputPath and returns a compact summary. Does not alter an open browser project.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__airpocket_studio__studio_analyze(args: {
  method?: "wasm-pcg" | "pcg" | "pcg-strict" | "mfem-wasm";
  operation?: "solve" | "mesh";
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  outputPath: string;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  path: string;
  size?: number;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Apply a reviewed STEP CAD replacement using exact input and replacement revisions, preserving physical setup and requiring confirmation of old provenance. Unmatched conditions remain pending and block analysis. Exclusively publishes a distinct new JSON; never overwrites input, replacement or an existing output.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__airpocket_studio__studio_apply_cad_update(args: {
  expectedReplacementRevision: string;
  expectedRevision: string;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  outputPath: string;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  path: string;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  replacementPath: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Evaluate fatigue or Mode-I fracture screening from a saved structural elastic analysis using its recorded material evidence and explicit options. Requires the exact result revision; publishes a distinct new analysis JSON without overwriting files. Does not infer missing material data or claim failure probability.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__airpocket_studio__studio_assess_result(args: {
  expectedResultRevision: string;
  kind: "fatigue" | "fracture";
  options: { [key: string]: unknown; };
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  outputPath: string;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  path: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Read validated fatigue/fracture screening metadata (or available:false with its result revision before evaluation) and a bounded element page (default 50, maximum 200) from a saved analysis. Optional exact result revision prevents reading a different version. Does not write files.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__airpocket_studio__studio_assessment(args: {
  expectedResultRevision?: string;
  kind: "fatigue" | "fracture";
  limit?: number;
  offset?: number;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  path: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Create a new project with an explicit built-in source: box(bounds), boxes(boxes), fixed cylinder(kind only), sphere(center/radius), tube(center/axis/innerRadius/outerRadius/length), using mm. No material values or boundary conditions are invented.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__airpocket_studio__studio_create_builtin_project(args: {
  name?: string;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  outputPath: string;
  source: { [key: string]: unknown; };
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Read stable diagnostics for unsupported execution combinations and the selected observation profile for a saved project. The selected profile is a declaration, not evidence that a job emitted it. Geometry, units, constraints and material completeness still require full validation. Includes actual Node host metadata and observed-risk diagnostics, not runtime safety certification.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__airpocket_studio__studio_diagnose_execution(args: {
  adaptive?: boolean;
  includeFields?: boolean;
  method?: "wasm-pcg" | "pcg" | "pcg-strict" | "mfem-wasm";
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  path: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Atomically apply semantic setup operations to saved JSON and publish a new outputPath. Requires the revision from studio_inspect_project; stale revisions and unsupported methods are rejected. Never alters the input or an open browser. Returns a compact summary, not the full model.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__airpocket_studio__studio_edit_project(args: {
  // Optional exact resulting input revision from studio_preview_edit; rejects a different transaction result before publication.
  expectedResultingRevision?: string;
  expectedRevision: string;
  operations: Array<{ args: Array<string>; method: "selectTriangles" | "selectCadFace" | "selectPlanarRegion" | "selectCylindricalRegion" | "clearSelection" | "addCondition" | "removeCondition" | "selectCondition" | "replaceConditionRegion" | "reapplyConditionRegion" | "setMaterial" | "setMaterialProperties" | "setMaterialPreset" | "applyCatalogMaterial" | "setStudy" | "setMeshSettings" | "setInputProvenance" | "setAnalysisIntent"; }>;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  outputPath: string;
  // Absolute local JSON file path
  path: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Read a local 3MF or linear G-code file up to 50,000,000 bytes and exclusively publish a distinct new parsed print JSON. Interprets geometry and possible deposition paths without sending commands to hardware or inferring strength. Returns compact revisioned metadata, not geometry arrays.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
